cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its data, please cite both the Zenodo deposit and the associated article."
title: "lfspin: light-front spin dynamics, exact benchmarks and physics-informed neural network solver"
abstract: >-
  Code and data for the article "Rapidity-Coupled Spin Dynamics in Pulsed Laser
  Fields: Exact Light-Front Solutions, Numerical Benchmarks, and
  Physics-Informed Neural Networks". For an electron in a linearly
  polarized plane-wave laser pulse the rest-frame polarization angle follows the
  instantaneous vector potential exactly, so the net spin rotation vanishes for
  every carrier-envelope phase. The package verifies this closed form against a
  light-front DOP853 reference, scans the carrier-envelope phase, benchmarks
  lab-time RK4, Boris-BMT, Higuera-Cary-BMT and light-front RK4 integrators, and
  trains a physics-informed neural network on the light-front orbital and BMT
  equations, including an elliptically polarized pulse for which no closed-form solution is
  known. It also maps the CEP sensitivity over amplitude and pulse length and
  follows the net post-pulse rotation from linear to circular polarization. It contains the computed results, the trained networks and the figures.
